\f0\b Request: 
\f1\b0 I am a process engineer at a manufacturing plant, and I need to choose which of three candidate centrifugal pumps should replace the failing cooling water pump, so the plant manager can approve the purchase. I will use Visual Studio Code with a Jupyter notebook to calculate the pipe system head loss from the piping data, build the system curve, overlay each pump's manufacturer curve, find each operating point, and check the NPSH margin for cavitation risk. I will compare the pumps by flow delivered, efficiency and yearly energy cost. I will use PowerPoint to present the comparison and my recommended pump in a short briefing exported to PDF, and Microsoft Word to complete a one page pump data sheet for procurement.\
\

\f0\b Task Description: 
\f1\b0\
1. Read the customer requirement note in Microsoft Word to confirm the duty, the piping and the acceptance rules.\
2. In Visual Studio Code, load the pump curves and piping data, calculate head loss and verify it by hand, build the system curve, find each pump's operating point, check NPSH margin, energy cost and five year cost, then apply the customer's rules to choose the pump.\
3. Build a three slide PowerPoint briefing with the pump curve chart, the comparison table and the recommendation, and export it to PDF.\
4. Complete the Word pump data sheet for procurement with the selected pump values, the checks, the result and the limits.\
5. Cross-check the final numbers against the notebook in Visual Studio Code.\
